KNOWNBUG: N5008 [class.copy.elis]/[class.copy.ctor] -- returning a local
by value mis-handles a move constructor that BRANCHES on the source's
self-pointer state: the constructed destination is clobbered by a
bitwise copy, leaving the pointer member targeting the return-value
temporary's buffer (dead object).  The SSO shape: breaks std::string
returned by value (t.front() reads a dead object), which blocks the
strip_string unit proof (regression/unit-proofs/strip_string).
Header-free, 25 essential lines, reduced from the std::string trace;
g++/clang++ runtime-verified.  Flip to CORE when fixed.
